@startbpmn BP07_CheckOutAGoal
lang en

output L1 "01_detailed/BP07_CheckOutAGoal.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP07_CheckOutAGoal.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - what a goal check-out captures, and that it is available at any time: BR-27, QB-32
'   - per-measure status is auto-inferred by measure type: BR-28
'   - the user may override any inferred status, a boolean to Partial included: BR-29
'   - closing actions: archive the goal default ON, follow-up default OFF: BR-30
'   - overriding an inferred status is a FIELD of the sitting, like the outcome and the retro,
'     not a decision of its own: BR-29, SA 2026-10-11
'   - the write does not re-ask what the request carries: what the reach said rides with it,
'     the way every sibling cascade carries "the ones the user included": SA 2026-10-11
'   - what carry-forward inherits, resets and back-references: BR-31
'   - unfinished input is a draft, forms included: the field drafts as it is filled in, and the
'     operation that keeps it is drawn ONCE, in BP19, not per editing process. Here it is a
'     bound rule on the step that fills the field: BR-121, SA 2026-10-11
'   - the check-out shape is observed, reflect, judge, opt-in closing actions, one gesture: BR-39
'   - archiving counts archived descendants too: BR-117
'   - an archived goal is frozen, so it cannot be checked out: BR-05, SA 2026-10-10
'   - a step never enumerates the fields a request stores: which fields the entity carries is
'     a Detail Design matter and is not known yet, so the step names the act and its subject
'     only: SA 2026-10-14
'   - the archiving at check-out is NOT the disclose-and-approve gesture. The sitting presents the
'     goal's linked projects, every one of them picked to go with it, and the user leaves active
'     whichever should stay; what it picks rides on the completing write, which is what confirms.
'     There is no second cycle and nothing is approved twice. The informed approval stays with an
'     EXPLICIT archiving request, where the goal is archived on its own and the cascade is all it
'     is about (BP05). This retires the three-answer reach question of SA 2026-10-11 and
'     SA 2026-10-16 together with the disclosure it approved: call site BP07.03 (See what archiving
'     the goal takes) is RETIRED, its id never reused: BR-30, BR-112, ADR-066, SA 2026-10-17
'   - the linked projects arrive with what the check-out starts from, the one read this sitting
'     makes: the Goals view does not carry them, and the archiving cannot be settled without them:
'     BR-112, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-17
'   - an archived goal cannot be checked out at all, so no path of this drawing is about one: the
'     check-out is reached from the Goals view, which carries the live goals, and the write verifies
'     what it is handed. The read answers no freeze and no gateway stands in front of the sitting.
'     This retires the frozen answer and the archived path it fed: BR-05, BR-87, BR-128,
'     SA 2026-10-17
'   - taking the inferred statuses as they stand is not an act: that branch carries no box and its
'     edge runs straight to the notes: SA 2026-10-17
'   - the SITTING HOLDS EVERY DECISION and ONE request carries them all: the surface offers every
'     option - the outcome, the statuses, the notes, the archiving reach, whether to create a
'     follow-up - and the system then stores the check-out, archives, creates the follow-up and
'     reports the outcome in one go. Nothing is decided after the last gesture; a decision at the
'     tail would be legitimate only on information that did not exist earlier, and there is none.
'     Editing the follow-up is NOT part of the check-out: once it exists it is a goal like any
'     other and BP05's editor amends it. This retires call sites BP07.05 (Seed a follow-up goal)
'     and BP07.06 (Create the follow-up goal), their ids never reused, together with the seed read,
'     the review and the commit-or-abandon gateway: what the follow-up inherits is BR-31's and
'     needs no round trip. The completing act is a gateway edge's target now, so it carries a
'     handle: BR-30, BR-31, BR-39, ADR-066, SA 2026-10-17
'   - PICKING THE DRAFT UP is not modelled here, no more than keeping it is. It is the drafting UX
'     and it holds for every content edit in the product, so a step per edit carries no value, and
'     neither the request nor its answer names it any more: a half-written sitting is there when the
'     user comes back because BP19 keeps it, not because this chain fetches it: BR-32, BR-121,
'     SA 2026-10-17 ("rename and drop draft")
'   - a task box is a return target and nothing else: SA 2026-10-16
'   - nothing re-reads the goal or its measures: they came with the goals (BP05.01) and a view is
'     read whole, so what the system has to answer here is what it OBSERVED - the status it infers
'     per measure. There is no proposal in it: the system
'     observes and the user judges: BR-28, BR-29, BR-39, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-16 ("a proposal does
'     not make any sense to me")
'   - NOTHING IS FETCHED HERE. Every record is loaded once, at start-up (BP01), so a step that only
'     went to the store is gone, and one that selects or qualifies what the act works on says so
'     instead of saying read. What a chain still asks the system for is what it COMPUTES, which is
'     business and stays out of the client. When data is read is a detail design decision:
'     BR-128, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-17 ("when we will read data is not a business concern, but a
'     detail design decision ... I rule that this will be done once at startup")
'
'   - THE PROCESS IS CHECKING A GOAL OUT, and its name says so: the act is a check-out everywhere
'     else in the drawing - the sitting, the record, the gesture that completes it - and the file,
'     the id's name half and the request now read the same way. The call-site id BP07.04 is
'     untouched, a name being descriptive and an id never renamed: ADR-066, SA 2026-10-17
'     ("rename BP07 to CheckOutAGoal")
'
' Scope: this process judges one goal and ends its cycle. Framing and maintaining the goal is BP05,
' its progress measures are BP06. Archiving a goal without checking it out is BP05's: the two acts
' are independent, and this one only offers archiving as a closing action.
'
' Call-site collapsing: the per-measure judgment is not a chain of its own. The statuses arrive
' with what the system observed and leave with the close-out; overriding one changes what the user
' submits, not which operation is called. The archiving reach is the same: the projects picked are
' a field of the sitting, carried by the completing write, and so is the follow-up: whether to
' create one is a flag on that one request.

pool "User" {
  start "A cycle ending, or a commitment to settle"
  :Open a goal's check-out;
  send "Read the inferred statuses and the linked projects" to observedIn
  receive "A status inferred per measure, and the goal's linked projects" as observed

  :Rate the overall outcome;
  note "Achieved, partially achieved, missed or abandoned. The outcome is required; everything else in the sitting is optional."

  if "Accept the inferred statuses?" rule BR-29 then "override one"
    :Set a status by hand;
    multiInstance
    note "Any inferred status can be overridden, a boolean measure set to Partial included. The rule constrains the inference, never the judgment."
  else "take them as they are"
    goto notes
  endif

  task "Write the goal notes" as notes
  multiInstance
  rule BR-32
  rule BR-121

  if "What becomes of the goal?" rule BR-30 then "archive it"
    :Pick which linked projects go with it;
    multiInstance
    rule BR-112
    note "The linked projects come with the check-out, every one of them picked to go with the goal, and whichever should stay is left active. An archived goal still exists, so a project kept active is not orphaned. The goal's progress measures and their check-in history go with it unasked."
  else "leave it active"
    :Turn the archive action off;
  endif

  if "Carry the commitment forward?" rule BR-30 then "yes"
    :Ask for a follow-up;
    rule BR-31
    note "What a follow-up inherits, resets and back-references is fixed, so the sitting says only whether to create one. Amending it afterwards is editing a goal, on the goals view."
  else "no, end it here"
    goto complete
  endif

  task "Complete the check-out" as complete
  send "Check the goal out" to closeIn
  receive "The check-out outcome" as closed
  note "One request carries everything the sitting decided, and the system executes it in one go: the check-out stored, the archiving where it was asked for, the follow-up created, the outcome reported. Nothing is left to decide after it."

  end "Commitment settled"
}

system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Inferred statuses requested" as observedIn
  call "BP07.01_ReadTheInferredStatuses" "Read the inferred statuses and the linked projects" {
    :Infer a status per measure from its current type, over the check-ins recorded under it;
    rule BR-28
    rule BR-29
    :Take the projects parented on the goal and on its measures;
    rule BR-112
    :Report collected information;
    rule BR-39
  }
  send "A status inferred per measure, and the goal's linked projects" to observed
  note "This is what the system observed, which the user then judges: the statuses are inferred and never decided. The goal and its measures came with the goals, so nothing re-reads them; their linked projects did not, and the sitting settles the archiving on them. A check-out is available at any time, with or without a horizon."
  end "Inferred statuses answered"

  messageStart "Close-out submitted" as closeIn
  call "BP07.04_CheckOutGoal" "Check the goal out" {
    :Store the check-out on the goal;
    rule BR-27
    :Archive the goal with its check-out record and the projects the user picked, where the check-out says so;
    rule BR-112
    rule BR-23
    :Create the follow-up from the goal and the check-out, linked back to it, where the sitting asked for one;
    rule BR-31
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The check-out outcome" to closed
  note "The check-out record stays attached to the goal, archived or not, and unarchiving never revokes it. The follow-up inherits the theme and the linked ideas, carries the objective over as a continuation, takes the Partial and Missed measures with their progress reset, advances a horizon that existed, drops the check-out notes, and keeps the link back to the check-out that keeps the iteration chain traceable."
  end "Close-out answered"
}

@endbpmn
